<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is Pakistan backing anti-Taliban groups in Afghanistan?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f08b81c93b94c69efd72d108ea5eb84f91dc22565b263b4e4a8a78379de5e26b</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814--1a7b1c3175b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban rulers in Afghanistan have accused Pakistan of aiding and sheltering armed resistance groups. The allegations come amid heightened tensions and are likely to deepen the rift between the two neighbors.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar genocide ruling: Rohingya say struggle for justice not over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b2d101642fe7bab9035e8653e5ee8706e0c012ee79fba5c2fa9476ac0e9746b</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365--347a55d37759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ has held Myanmar responsible for genocide against the Rohingya and ordered restitution and reparations. Community members have hailed the ruling, but caution that achieving real change will be long and hard.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: Pakistani minister visits Delhi for SCO forum amid frozen ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f5794a2a08849289a3223daa0a367516bf20baba83d87b43a0c0d2c329ef881</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-pakistani-minister-visits-delhi-for-sco-forum-amid-frozen-ties/live-79999264--d096d9f0fd84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-pakistani-minister-visits-delhi-for-sco-forum-amid-frozen-ties/live-79999264?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistan's Climate Minister Musadik Malik has arrived in New Delhi for an SCO cultural forum, the first visit by a Pakistani federal minister since 2023. Meanwhile, Cyclone Akvan has made landfall.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi praises 'turnaround' in relationship with Australia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47f7a3f6dadae88199246414036ec86124b3f55aa8a5926ba45647fb2ff4482a</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-praises-turnaround-in-relationship-with-australia/a-79999229--091456c7e1ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-praises-turnaround-in-relationship-with-australia/a-79999229?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The leaders of Australia and China have held talks on sidelines of APEC summit. Australian PM Anthony Albanese is also slated to meet Chinese Premier Li Qiang.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin have held trilateral talks ― but what did they achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4a042768661bddd5fb55184d575440ad21b819a35fb56ec697afad958fe3f4f</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/xi-jinping-donald-trump-and-vladimir-putin-have-held-trilateral-talks-_-but-what-did-they-achieve/a-79996668--6af4ec68160a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/xi-jinping-donald-trump-and-vladimir-putin-have-held-trilateral-talks-―-but-what-did-they-achieve/a-79996668?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The presidents of China, the US and Russia have held an unprecedented summit. While Trump said the three leaders were "making history," Xi described the talks as "fruitful" and Putin called them "open and candid."</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan minister to visit India, but no breakthrough expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbad263e975361b7896f254012d1320aaf7ca81c01983c492315e060ecb5ce60</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717--07503556e8b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani minister's visit to India for a Shanghai Cooperation Organization forum marks a rare high-level contact between the two archrivals, but analysts say it does not signal a resumption of bilateral engagement.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>APEC summit: Trump, Xi, Putin talks end with 'peace declaration'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2d8be1d331260a319888d8140fd86efaeb04faa6bf30880a945e7ad3e784207</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-trump-xi-putin-talks-end-with-peace-declaration/live-79964719--35792a5d6dfa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-trump-xi-putin-talks-end-with-peace-declaration/live-79964719?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The three world leaders discussed the Russian invasion of Ukraine as well as nuclear arms controls. Following the trilateral talks, President Trump reportedly headed to the airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar committed genocide against Rohingya, top UN court rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c50850a557546c6aea5acbc34e5538188ba6891470998439c045f13b1fccb54</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T11:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-committed-genocide-against-rohingya-top-un-court-rules/a-79987898--1622af9cbda3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-committed-genocide-against-rohingya-top-un-court-rules/a-79987898?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Court of Justice has upheld large parts of a genocide case against Myanmar linked to the 2017 conflict with its Rohingya minority. It called for it to pay reparations and let refugees return safely.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Nearly 50,000 evacuated as Cyclone Akvan nears the coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d6425fbd9b99a19ed5bab79305320c593588b6fcf728693a3585f9205d54583</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-nearly-50-000-evacuated-as-cyclone-akvan-nears-the-coast/live-79987334--51fef60fd516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-nearly-50-000-evacuated-as-cyclone-akvan-nears-the-coast/live-79987334?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cyclone Akvan, the third severe storm to hit India's east coast in a month, is expected to make landfall on November 20. Meanwhile, PM Modi led a meeting of his Council of Ministers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fc1230a9b4b6eccf5b28998471636109e173b8673d5ef0e25549390734ac5f</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New facilities in Laos and Cambodia: Is China expanding its military presence in Southeast Asia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f23084f70e15045c38c90d9620f3e48e3b151aa8b24fbffc3df3dd43fe5d921</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798--c731be0f2b99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has been growing its economic relationships in Southeast Asia. Now new military facilities in Laos and Cambodia are causing smaller countries to worry China's military networks are also expanding.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China faces Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca2b14490249e0b6885f377f21b3b84b934bb41c3bcf7a4a1c35fe5b5326d5a5</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--86131bd0e961.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Russia, Beijing is risking its image on the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
